Package: surveymixr
Type: Package
Title: Growth Mixture Models with Complex Survey Design
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2025-11-08
Authors@R: c(
    person("Siyang", "Ni", email = "johnni.nj@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Maintainer: Siyang Ni <johnni.nj@gmail.com>
Description: Implements growth mixture modeling (GMM) for longitudinal data with
    full integration of complex survey design features including stratification,
    clustering, and probability weights. Supports continuous, binary, ordinal,
    and count outcomes. Provides comprehensive model selection tools including
    Bootstrap Likelihood Ratio Test (BLRT), Lo-Mendell-Rubin test (LMR), and
    cross-validation. Features advanced diagnostics (influence detection,
    separation checks, residual analysis), data validation, and interactive
    visualizations. Implements the R3STEP approach for auxiliary variable analysis
    with classification uncertainty correction. This package fills a critical gap
    by enabling rigorous analyses of large-scale longitudinal surveys (e.g.,
    Millennium Cohort Study, Add Health, NLSY, ECLS) that were previously only
    possible in proprietary software like Mplus. Methods based on Muthén and
    Muthén (2017) <https://www.statmodel.com/>, Asparouhov and Muthén (2014)
    <doi:10.1080/10705511.2014.915181>, and Vermunt (2010)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1467-985X.2009.00626.x>.
